
  # Release Polish Plan — rusty-comms                                                                                 
                                                                                                                      
  **Branch:** chore/release-polish                                                                                    
  **Base:** main                                                                                                      
  **Status:** Complete                                                                                                
  **Date:** 2026-06-30                                                                                                
                                                                                                                      
  --------                                                                                                            
                                                                                                                      
  ## Objective                                                                                                        
                                                                                                                      
  Comprehensive code quality review and polish of the rusty-comms IPC benchmark                                       
  suite in preparation for initial release. Focus areas: code quality, efficiency,                                    
  cleanup, minor bug fixes, and issue creation for larger problems.                                                   
                                                                                                                      
  --------                                                                                                            
                                                                                                                      
  ## Review Groups                                                                                                    
                                                                                                                      
  The codebase was reviewed in 7 logical groups, each examined by a dedicated                                         
  review pass analyzing every file for bugs, performance issues, dead code,                                           
  style violations, and documentation accuracy.                                                                       
                                                                                                                      
   Group                            | Files                                       | Status                            
  ----------------------------------|---------------------------------------------|---------------------------------  
   1. Core types                    | ipc/mod.rs, execution_mode.rs, cli.rs       | Done                              
   2. Transport implementations     | 10 files in src/ipc/ (~8.6K lines)          | Done                              
   3. Benchmark runners             | benchmark.rs, benchmark_blocking.rs         | Done                              
   4. Results and metrics           | results.rs, results_blocking.rs, metrics.rs | Done                              
   5. Standalone client/server      | standalone_server.rs, standalone_client.rs  | Done                              
   6. Main and utilities            | main.rs, utils.rs, lib.rs, logging.rs       | Done                              
   7. Tests and examples            | Integration tests, unit test quality        | Done                              
                                                                                                                      
  --------                                                                                                            
                                                                                                                      
  ## Inline Fixes Applied                                                                                             
                                                                                                                      
  ### Bug Fixes                                                                                                       
                                                                                                                      
   File                                | Issue                               | Fix                                    
  -------------------------------------|-------------------------------------|--------------------------------------  
   src/cli.rs                          | parse_duration_micros silently      | Changed to Duration::from_secs_f64()   
                                       | truncated fractional values (e.g.   | with appropriate divisors, matching    
                                       | "1.5ms") due to as u64 cast         | parse_duration()                       
   src/ipc/unix_domain_socket_blocking | writev partial-write fallback used  | Rewrote to handle partial length-      
   .rs                                 | incorrect offset calculation        | prefix and partial payload cases       
                                       | (written.saturating_sub(4)) — could | separately; added writev == 0 error    
                                       | corrupt frames when written < 4     | handling                               
   src/ipc/tcp_socket.rs               | panic! in multi-server accept loop  | Replaced with warn! + continue to      
                                       | when try_clone() fails              | keep server running                    
   src/ipc/shared_memory_direct.rs     | No validation of payload_len read   | Added bounds check against             
                                       | from shared memory before           | MAX_PAYLOAD_SIZE with proper mutex     
                                       | copy_nonoverlapping — potential OOB | cleanup on failure                     
                                       | read                                |                                        
   src/ipc/shared_memory_direct.rs     | receive_blocking_timed captured a   | Changed to return the in-message       
                                       | new timestamp instead of using the  | timestamp for accurate latency         
                                       | already-captured                    | measurement                            
                                       | msg.receive_time_ns                 |                                        
   src/ipc/shared_memory_blocking.rs   | read_data_blocking did not reject   | Added zero-length rejection to match   
                                       | data_len == 0 (inconsistent with    | protocol validation                    
                                       | other transports)                   |                                        
   src/results.rs                      | get_memory_gb() hardcoded 16.0 —    | Replaced with actual /proc/meminfo     
                                       | incorrect system metadata in JSON   | read on Linux                          
                                       | output                              |                                        
   src/results.rs                      | SystemInfo::default() hardcoded     | Changed to use get_memory_gb() and     
                                       | rust_version: "1.75.0" and          | env!("CARGO_PKG_RUST_VERSION")         
                                       | memory_gb: 16.0                     |                                        
   src/results_blocking.rs             | Same hardcoded get_memory_gb()      | Same /proc/meminfo fix                 
                                       | returning 16.0                      |                                        
                                                                                                                      
  ### Performance Fixes                                                                                               
                                                                                                                      
   File        | Issue                                           | Fix                                                
  -------------|-------------------------------------------------|--------------------------------------------------  
   src/main.rs | .context(format!(...)) eagerly allocates format | Changed to .with_context(|| format!(...)) (lazy    
               | string on every call                            | evaluation)                                        
                                                                                                                      
  ### Code Cleanup                                                                                                    
                                                                                                                      
   File                      | Issue                                     | Fix                                        
  ---------------------------|-------------------------------------------|------------------------------------------  
   src/ipc/mod.rs            | Message::new() and                        | Made new_for_blocking delegate to new()    
                             | Message::new_for_blocking() were          | with #[inline] — semantic alias            
                             | identical implementations                 |                                            
   src/ipc/mod.rs            | Test                                      | Moved inside the test module               
                             | test_timestamp_offset_update_in_serialize |                                            
                             | d_buffer was outside mod tests {} block   |                                            
   src/ipc/mod.rs            | Test test_message_size_analysis used      | Replaced with proper assertions            
                             | println!                                  |                                            
   src/benchmark_blocking.rs | if true { ... } dead scaffolding wrapping | Removed the dead conditional               
                             | round-trip recording                      |                                            
   src/utils.rs              | Dead function current_timestamp_ns()      | Removed function and unused imports        
                             | (unused — callers use                     |                                            
                             | MessageLatencyRecord::current_timestamp_n |                                            
                             | s())                                      |                                            
   src/main.rs               | Stale dev comment // === ALL EXISTING     | Removed                                    
                             | MAIN() LOGIC STARTS HERE ===              |                                            
                                                                                                                      
  ### Style / Documentation Fixes                                                                                     
                                                                                                                      
   File                            | Issue                                   | Fix                                    
  ---------------------------------|-----------------------------------------|--------------------------------------  
   src/ipc/unix_domain_socket.rs   | println! in backpressure test           | Changed to tracing::trace!             
   src/ipc/tcp_socket.rs           | println! in backpressure test           | Changed to tracing::trace!             
   src/ipc/shared_memory.rs        | println! in backpressure test           | Changed to tracing::trace!             
   src/ipc/posix_message_queue.rs  | println! in backpressure test           | Changed to tracing::trace!             
   src/ipc/shared_memory_direct.rs | Module doc said #[repr(C, packed)] but  | Fixed to #[repr(C)]                    
                                   | struct is #[repr(C)]                    |                                        
   src/ipc/shared_memory_direct.rs | Comment said "Maximum 1MB" but          | Updated to "Maximum 8 KB"              
                                   | MAX_PAYLOAD_SIZE is 8 KB                |                                        
   src/main.rs                     | Doc said "No streaming output support   | Updated to reflect current state       
                                   | (will be added in Stage 5)" — streaming |                                        
                                   | is implemented                          |                                        
   src/benchmark_blocking.rs       | Same stale "Stage 5" streaming doc      | Updated                                
   src/lib.rs                      | "Zero-copy serialization" claim         | Changed to "Compact binary             
                                   | (bincode allocates; only SHM-direct is  | serialization via bincode"             
                                   | zero-copy)                              |                                        
   src/lib.rs                      | "Async I/O throughout using Tokio"      | Updated to mention both modes          
                                   | ignores blocking mode                   |                                        
   src/lib.rs                      | Warmup comment cited "JIT compilation"  | Changed to CPU cache/TLB warming       
                                   | (not applicable to AOT Rust)            |                                        
   src/logging.rs                  | Module docs described a non-existent    | Rewrote to describe actual exports     
                                   | init_logging function with usage        | (ColorizedFormatter)                   
                                   | example                                 |                                        
   src/results.rs                  | rust_version field doc said "compiler   | Fixed doc and method comment           
                                   | version" — it's actually MSRV           |                                        
                                                                                                                      
